# Subtest: RebalanceCoordinator blocks stale ADD when authoritative topology already satisfies target
    ok 1 - createOperation should fail closed when authoritative topology already satisfies the target replica count
    ok 2 - stale planner adds should surface the target-satisfied reason
    ok 3 - topology guard should preserve the canonical distinct-node count in diagnostics
    ok 4 - stale planner add should not persist a replica operation
    1..4
ok 6 - RebalanceCoordinator blocks stale ADD when authoritative topology already satisfies target # time=28.915ms

# Subtest: RebalanceCoordinator blocks REPLACE when target node already has partition topology
    ok 1 - createOperation should fail closed when REPLACE targets an occupied partition node
    ok 2 - duplicate replacement target rows should surface the occupied-target reason
    ok 3 - blocked replacement topology creation should not persist a replica operation
    1..3
ok 7 - RebalanceCoordinator blocks REPLACE when target node already has partition topology # time=23.886ms

# Subtest: RebalanceCoordinator applies topology occupancy guard to message-group creates
    ok 1 - message-group ADD should use the shared topology occupancy guard
    ok 2 - message-group duplicate topology should surface the occupied-target reason
    ok 3 - blocked message-group topology creation should not persist a replica operation
    1..3
ok 8 - RebalanceCoordinator applies topology occupancy guard to message-group creates # time=20.992ms

# Subtest: count-keyed lane HOLDS a REPLACE churn create while the critical partition is over target on alive replicas (red-on-revert: the rows-only ADD guard exempts REPLACE, so without the hold the churn is admitted)
    ok 1 - over-target REPLACE churn is rejected by the count-keyed lane hold
    ok 2 - the held REPLACE churn create persists no replica operation
    1..2
ok 9 - count-keyed lane HOLDS a REPLACE churn create while the critical partition is over target on alive replicas (red-on-revert: the rows-only ADD guard exempts REPLACE, so without the hold the churn is admitted) # time=25.328ms

# Subtest: count-keyed lane consumes canonical identity deduplication
    ok 1 - duplicate observations of one identity do not manufacture a surplus
    ok 2 - critical lane output depends on canonical inventory deduplication
    1..2
ok 10 - count-keyed lane consumes canonical identity deduplication # time=43.865ms

# Subtest: count-keyed lane ALIVE-GUARD: a FAILED replica does not count toward the alive occupancy, so a legitimate re-placement REPLACE is admitted (the hold never over-blocks a dead-replica fix)
    ok 1 - alive-occupancy at target (failed replica excluded) admits the re-placement REPLACE
    1..1
ok 11 - count-keyed lane ALIVE-GUARD: a FAILED replica does not count toward the alive occupancy, so a legitimate re-placement REPLACE is admitted (the hold never over-blocks a dead-replica fix) # time=28.87ms

# Subtest: count-keyed lane HOLDS a REPLACE churn create when the surplus is a draining (REMOVING) source -- the real over-replication signature: 3 active + 1 removing source on ready nodes is over target
    ok 1 - a draining (removing) source keeps the partition over target -> churn create is held
    ok 2 - the held churn create persists no replica operation
    1..2
ok 12 - count-keyed lane HOLDS a REPLACE churn create when the surplus is a draining (REMOVING) source -- the real over-replication signature: 3 active + 1 removing source on ready nodes is over target # time=22.769ms

